japanese-wikimedia holds words of Japanese Wikipedia article titles and their readings, from Japanese Wikipedia (https://ja.wikipedia.org/), by Wikipedia contributors, and Japanese set phrases (四字熟語, 慣用句, ことわざ) and their readings, from the English and the Japanese Wiktionary (https://en.wiktionary.org/, https://ja.wiktionary.org/), by Wiktionary contributors, as extracted by wiktextract (https://kaikki.org/), all under CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/). The kanji readings that check them come from KANJIDIC2 (Electronic Dictionary Research and Development Group, https://www.edrdg.org/, CC BY-SA 4.0). This pack is shared under CC BY-SA 4.0.
